# 53. Production JVM options

A reasonable starting point for modern Java might look like:

```bash
java \
-Xms4g \
-Xmx4g \
-XX:+UseG1GC \
-XX:MaxGCPauseMillis=200 \
-Xlog:gc*:file=/var/log/app/gc.log:time,uptime,level,tags \
-jar application.jar
```

But these numbers are **not universal**.

For example:

```text
4 GB heap
```

may be appropriate for one service and completely wrong for another.

Tune based on:

```text
traffic
allocation rate
object lifetime
CPU
