# 54. Kubernetes consideration

This is extremely important for modern Spring Boot applications.

Suppose Kubernetes container:

```text
Memory limit = 4 GB
```

and you configure:

```bash
-Xmx4g
```

That's dangerous.

Why?

Because JVM process memory isn't only heap.

You also have:

```text
Heap
+
Metaspace
+
Thread stacks
+
Code cache
+
Direct buffers
+
Native memory
```

Therefore:

```text
Container memory
      |
      +-- Heap
      +-- Metaspace
      +-- Threads
      +-- Native
      +-- Direct buffers
```

The container can be OOM-killed even when:

```text
Java heap < Xmx
```

---

# 55. Better container sizing concept

For example:

```text
Container limit = 4 GB

Heap = maybe 2.5–3 GB
Remaining =
    Metaspace
    Threads
    Direct memory
    Native
    JVM overhead
```

Exact sizing depends on the workload.

You can also use:

```bash
-XX:MaxRAMPercentage=70
```

instead of hardcoding heap size, depending on your deployment model.

