# 56. Heap Dump vs Thread Dump vs GC Logs

This is the interview answer you should remember:

### Heap Dump

> A heap dump is a snapshot of objects in JVM heap at a particular point in time. It is primarily used to investigate memory leaks, excessive memory consumption, large collections, caches, and object retention.

### Thread Dump

> A thread dump is a snapshot of JVM threads and their states. It is primarily used to investigate deadlocks, blocked threads, thread pool exhaustion, high CPU, stuck requests, and concurrency issues.

### GC Logs

> GC logs provide a historical record of garbage collection activity, including GC frequency, pause duration, heap occupancy before and after GC, and collector behavior. They are used to identify excessive allocation, frequent GC, long pauses, and memory-pressure problems.

